{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 38,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.128
          ],
          "content": "(iii) A quadrilateral whose diagonals bisect each other must be a parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.13,
            0.847,
            0.17
          ],
          "content": "(iv) A quadrilateral whose diagonals are perpendicular to each other must be a rhombus."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.173,
            0.847,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "(v) A quadrilateral in which the opposite angles are equal must be a parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.215,
            0.846,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "(vi) A quadrilateral in which all the angles are equal is a rectangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.239,
            0.648,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "(vii) Isosceles trapeziums are parallelograms."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.263,
            0.204,
            0.28
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Ans."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.28,
            0.847,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": "(i) False. In a square the diagonals are also perpendicular to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.192,
            0.322,
            0.847,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "(ii) True. The fourth angle will also be equal to 90°, because sum of all angles is equal to 360°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.365,
            0.304,
            0.386
          ],
          "content": "(iii) True"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.389,
            0.514,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": "(iv) False. It may be a Kite also."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.414,
            0.307,
            0.434
          ],
          "content": "(v) True."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.437,
            0.307,
            0.457
          ],
          "content": "(vi) True."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.181,
            0.461,
            0.813,
            0.483
          ],
          "content": "(vii) False. The other pair of opposite sides may not be parallel."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.867,
            0.926,
            0.881,
            0.941
          ],
          "content": "9"
        }
      ]
    }
